e previous stage, with `Z_rel` transporting a preserved relation along the iteration by induction on the stage. `sigmaJ` is (7.17). `eq_7_18_eq` is the equal-tag half of (7.18), \(\sigma_j^m(\{(j,0)\})=\{(j,m)\}\), by induction, the zero step being reflexivity and the successor step the singleton rule for \(\sigma_j\). `eq_7_18_ne` proves the distinct-tag half only for the \((m+1)\)-st iterate, which is bottom; the printed (7.18) writes the \(m\)-th iterate, which at \(m=0\) is the starting singleton. `eq_7_19` is the joint iteration of \(\sigma_j\cup\sigma_{j'}\), by the equal-tag rule when the tags agree and, when they differ, by induction through (2.9) and the two distinct-tag union rules. `plotkinE`, `plotkin_finite_separation`, and `plotkin_function_related` build the fresh-tag equivalence used in that uniqueness argument. `Basic`’s gloss says the file re-exports Theorems 7.1–7.4; the file imports these definitions and the syntax-directed interpreter (`LambTerm`, `Hinterp`, `Hcomb`) together with the retract lemmas `theorem_4_4_typed`, `theorem_4_4_med`, and `theorem_4_5_sum`. The modules `theorem_7_1`, `theorem_7_2`, `theorem_7_3`, and `theorem_7_4` are absent, so the closure, isomorphism, functionality, and iterator theorems are not proved in this note. `Icomb_isGraph`, `Kcomb_isGraph`, and `Scomb_isGraph` show only that those combinators equal the graphs of their own application. **Theorem:** partial — (7.1) is not formalized, the equivalence stays an external `Prop`, and Theorems 7.1–7.4 are outside the import list, while `arrowE`, `prodE`, `sumE`, `Ea`, `Nrel`, `Z`, `eq_7_18_eq`, `eq_7_18_ne`, and `eq_7_19` match the later displayed equations except for the off-by-one in the distinct-tag clause of (7.18). **Proof:** partial — symmetry and transitivity are proved inside each constructor, and (7.18)–(7.19) are proved by induction on the iterate, but this import list contains no proof of the four theorems the prose names, and `Basic` does not contain them.
